        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello! Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nCompletions for `:Git` command are already quite complex, so I am not very optimistic that this will be added. But would like to know the use case better to have more info before deciding.\n\nSo do I understand correctly that you'd like to type `:Git show main:`, then press `<Tab>`, and see paths as candidates? And do I understand correctly that you also want to be able to see among completion suggestions files that are already deleted from disk?\n\nMy currently suggested \"more interactive\" solution would be to execute `:Git diff`. This shows in separate tabpage the patch (very manageable with folds from 'mini.git') which should include the deleted file. Placing a cursor on deleted file and executing `show_at_cursor()` will show its content as if `:Git show :0:path/to/file`, which I *think* would work. Fair warning, it doesn't seem to work on `main`, but it will be fixed after fixing #2063.",
