        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Yeah, you got it. `Gedit` does this, and I have always found it quite handy (and impressive) that it can tab complete the file tree as it was for the git ref you have prepended.\n\nI tried your suggested approach (needed to do `Git diff HEAD~5` as the file was deleted some commits ago), but becasue the above commit isn't merged into the `main-git` repo yet, I hope it's okay if I test it after. As far as I can see from opening other files, I think this interactive solution would solve my use-case, even if it is a few more steps 😊 ",
