        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I tried your suggested approach (needed to do `Git diff HEAD~5` as the file was deleted some commits ago), but becasue the above commit isn't merged into the `main-git` repo yet, I hope it's okay if I test it after. As far as I can see from opening other files, I think this interactive solution would solve my use-case, even if it is a few more steps 😊\n\nThis should now work on latest `main`.\n\nAs making completion specifically for `git show main:` case *specifically* to enable this kind of workflow feels imbalanced (too much complexity, especially if deleted files need to be accounted for, for relatively niche use case), I am going to close this as not planned.\n\nI'd still ask you to please follow up on whether the suggested \"interactive solution\" works for you.",
